510:
A special one percent sales and use tax shall be imposed in the special district of Cook County for a period of time not to exceed six years and for the raising of an estimated amount of $12,600,000 for the purpose of:
(1) Funding capital outlay projects including road, streets and bridge projects, and public facility renovations, solid waste handling facility and equipment, recreation facility and equipment, capital outlay and debt service projects for economic development, Adel/Cook County Airport:
(2) For funding of capital outlay projects including road, streets and bridge projects, water, sewer and natural gas capital outlay, general capital outlay for the City of Adel;
(3) For funding of capital outlay projects including public water and sewer capital outlay, road, streets and bridge projects and equipment, recreational facility capital outlay and general capital outlay including police station facility and equipment, for the Town of Sparks;
(4) For funding of capital outlay projects including road, and street projects and equipment, and General Capital Outlay for the Town of Lenox;
(5) For funding capital outlay projects including road, and street projects including equipment, and general capital outlay for the Town of Cecil.
(Res. of 8-1-2016)

541:
In accordance with O.C.G.A. § 48-13-112(c), such excise tax shall be:
(1) Imposed only at the time sales and use tax on the sale or use of such energy would have been due and payable under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-30 but for the exemption under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-3.2;
(2) Due and payable in the same manner as would be required under O.C.G.A. § 48-8-1 et seq., except as other provided in O.C.G.A. § 48-8-110 et seq.;
(3) A debt of the purchaser of energy until it is paid and shall be recoverable at law in the same manner as authorized for the recovery of other debts;
(4) Remitted to the governing authority of Cook County by the dealer collecting such excise tax; and
(5) A liability of the dealer at the applicable rate on the charges actually collected or the amount of excise taxes collected from purchasers, whichever is greater.
(Ord. of 12-10-2012, § 4)
